<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karpuramanjari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 900 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karpuramanjari is a play written in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prakrit">Prakrit</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajashekhara">Rajashekhara</a>, court poet of the Gurjara-Pratihara kings at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a>, around 900 CE. A light romantic comedy of the type called sattaka, it tells of a king's love for the princess Karpuramanjari and his queen's jealousy. It is the best-known play composed entirely in Prakrit.</p></div>
